//
// The file lives in the `agreement` package for the sole reason that
// every interesting wire type (rawVote, unauthenticatedVote, vote,
// unauthenticatedBundle, bundle, voteAuthenticator,
// equivocationVoteAuthenticator, unauthenticatedProposal,
// transmittedPayload) is package-private. The fixtures themselves are
// deterministic, synthetic values whose crypto fields (VrfProof,
// OneTimeSignature, Credential) are filled with predictable byte
// patterns; we're probing canonical msgpack encoding, not signature
// validity.
//
// Output layout per wire type `T`:
//
//	<dir>/<subdir>/<name>.msgpack  -- raw protocol.Encode(&v) bytes
//	<dir>/<subdir>/<name>.json     -- metadata sidecar (JSON)
//
// `dir` is taken from the `ALGOD_RUST_WIRE_FIXTURE_DIR` env var. If
// unset, the test skips — so running `go test ./agreement/...`
// normally doesn't produce files.

